## Dance mode assets

`src/assets/RobotExpressive.glb` — model by Tomás Laulhé
(https://www.patreon.com/quaternius), released under CC0 1.0. Modifications by
Don McCurdy (https://donmccurdy.com/): three facial expression morph targets,
converted with FBX2GLTF, duplicate materials removed and material metalness
reduced. Obtained from the three.js repository
(examples/models/gltf/RobotExpressive/, r160).

Deliberately NOT the Soldier/Michelle/Xbot models used by other three.js
examples: those are Mixamo assets, credited individually rather than covered by
three.js's MIT licence, and Adobe's General Terms sec. 3.6 forbids distributing
Content Files "on a stand-alone basis, outside of the End Use" — which a .glb
committed to a public repository would be.

`src/vendor/three-addons.js` — GLTFLoader, BufferGeometryUtils and
SkeletonUtils from three.js r160 (MIT), converted from ES modules to a classic
script by `scripts/build-three-addons.mjs`. Regenerate with that script rather
than editing it.
